usage: j5_rbp_context.py [-h] [--encode-root ENCODE_ROOT]
                         [--index-dir INDEX_DIR] --out OUT
                         [--metadata METADATA]
                         [--queries QUERIES [QUERIES ...]]
                         [--query-list QUERY_LIST] [--sentinel]
                         [--require-query-done] [--fasta FASTA]
                         [--genes GENES]

J5: observed RBP context, with an accession-bound GRCh38 assembly fence. RBP
knockdown and local steric ASO inhibition are NOT interchangeable. KD events
always carry evidence_class='knockdown_not_steric_block', with a separate
measurement_evidence_class='observed'. No potency or outcome joins. Design:
disk-backed SQLite RTree partitions by RBP/cell/chromosome; files commit
individually, query Parquet streams in bounded batches, hits have explicit
caps. BED is 0-based half-open; public queries/J6/J8 footprints are 1-based
inclusive. Overlap uses the query strand only for +/- peaks. Signed nearest
distance is peak minus query (nearest BASES, hence adjacent=1), reversed on
minus-strand peaks; unstranded peaks use genomic orientation. Within each
RBP/cell, files form a union for presence, but signal measurements retain
accession/replicate identity. No signal averaging, replicate consensus, or
cross-cell pooling. A missing local file does not establish that an assay was
never performed. Refused/partial evidence cannot produce a False presence flag
after a miss. Metadata input: JSON mapping accession -> original ENCODE File
object. Its accession, @id and md5sum must match the local file. Assembly may
instead come from an explicit assembly=/genome= header; conflicting assertions
are refused. No inferred assemblies and no implicit liftover. Optional
sample1_role, sample2_role, sample_order_evidence document rMATS sample order;
absent these, raw sample1-minus-sample2 is observed, but KD direction remains
unavailable. Decoys are same-gene, length/GC matched coordinate shifts,
labelled proxy; they are descriptive background intervals, never verified
negative labels. Default fixed shifts are finite candidates, not a statistical
sampling universe. No p-values. Missing reference/gene bounds yields
unavailable controls. CLI: --encode-root ... --out ... [--metadata
encode_file_objects.json] [--queries shard.parquet ... | --query-list
ordered_paths.txt | --sentinel] [--fasta GRCh38.fa --genes gene_bounds.tsv]
Gene TSV: gene_id,chrom,start1,end1,strand,assembly,annotation. It is indexed
on disk; optional FASTA uses J6's pinned primary-contig length fence. A
sentinel uses three known F18/F14/F10 footprints plus the exon-7 anchor +/-500
kb window. Large production ingestion belongs in Slurm. Requeue restarts at
committed files and output shards. Changed inputs/code require a fresh output
directory.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --encode-root ENCODE_ROOT
  --index-dir INDEX_DIR
                        Reuse completed index read-only; no ingestion in this
                        job
  --out OUT
  --metadata METADATA
  --queries QUERIES [QUERIES ...]
  --query-list QUERY_LIST
  --sentinel
  --require-query-done
  --fasta FASTA
  --genes GENES

